    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "f8352c5a-c228-5742-a996-27e80b6c0565",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following statements are true regarding the matrix $R$ given below?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $R$ is a singular matrix\n- **II.** $R$ is **not** a singular matrix\n- **III.** $det(R)=0$\n\n$$\nR=\\begin{bmatrix}\\sqrt{3} & 0 & - \\frac{1}{2} \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & 2 & 0 \\\\ 6 & 0 & - \\sqrt{3}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Remember that a square matrix is singular if its determinant is equal to $0.$\n\nUsing the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(R) & =|\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3} & 0 & - \\frac{1}{2} \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & 2 & 0 \\\\ 6 & 0 & - \\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}|\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & - \\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}|+0|\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3} & 0 \\\\ 6 & - \\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}|+(- \\frac{1}{2})|\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3} & 2 \\\\ 6 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}(- 2 \\sqrt{3}+0)+0+(- \\frac{1}{2})(0-12) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}\\cdot (- 2 \\sqrt{3})+(- \\frac{1}{2})\\cdot (-12) \\\\  & =-6+6 \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $det(R)=0$, the matrix is singular. \n\nTherefore, only statements I and III are true.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "bc9802d5-5fe1-5c07-9ba5-90f9d54f0212",
          ":answer-field/key": "I",
